## 7. Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### Outdated Comments

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Comment doesn't match code
// Send email notification
await sendSlackMessage(user.slackId, message)  // Actually sends Slack!

// ✅ CORRECT - Keep comments in sync
// Send Slack notification
await sendSlackMessage(user.slackId, message)
```

### Commented-Out Code

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Dead code in comments
// const oldImplementation = async () => {
//   const result = await fetch('/api/old-endpoint')
//   return result.json()
// }

const newImplementation = async () => {
  return await fetch('/api/v2/endpoint').then(r => r.json())
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Remove dead code, use git history if needed
const fetchData = async () => {
  return await fetch('/api/v2/endpoint').then(r => r.json())
}
```

### TODOs Without Tickets

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Orphan TODO
// TODO: Fix this later
// TODO: Refactor this
// TODO: Handle edge cases

// ✅ CORRECT - TODO with tracking
// TODO(CEN-1234): Add retry logic for transient failures
// TODO(@username): Review security implications before launch
// FIXME(CEN-5678): Race condition when multiple users edit simultaneously
```

### Anti-Pattern Summary

| Anti-Pattern | Why It's Bad | Fix |
|--------------|--------------|-----|
| Outdated comments | Misleads readers, causes bugs | Update or remove |
| Commented-out code | Clutters codebase, confuses readers | Delete, use git |
| TODOs without tickets | Never get fixed, accumulate | Add ticket reference |
| Excessive comments | Noise reduces signal | Trust self-documenting code |
| Comments instead of code | Lazy fix for bad naming | Refactor to be clear |

## 8. Quick Checklist

Before committing any code:

### JSDoc
- [ ] All exported functions have JSDoc
- [ ] `@param` for each parameter with description
- [ ] `@returns` describes return value
- [ ] `@throws` lists all error conditions
- [ ] `@security` for auth-related functions
- [ ] `@audit` for logged operations

### Security Annotations
- [ ] `// SECURITY:` on rate limiting, attack prevention
- [ ] `// AUTH:` on permission checks
- [ ] `// AUDIT:` on logged operations
- [ ] `// RLS:` on queries relying on Row Level Security
- [ ] `// VALIDATION:` on input sanitization

### Business Logic
- [ ] Non-obvious business rules explained
- [ ] Magic numbers have explanatory comments
- [ ] State transitions documented
- [ ] Edge cases explained with reasoning
- [ ] Temporal constraints (cooldowns, TTLs) documented

### Component Documentation
- [ ] Complex components have `@component` JSDoc
- [ ] Usage examples provided
- [ ] State management explained
- [ ] Props documented

### Hygiene
- [ ] No commented-out code
- [ ] No orphan TODOs (all have ticket references)
- [ ] Comments match actual code behavior
- [ ] No comments on obvious/self-documenting code
- [ ] File headers on complex services

## Documentation Debt Warning Signs

If you encounter these, documentation is needed:

- "What does this function do?" - Add JSDoc
- "Why is this check here?" - Add `// SECURITY:` or business rule comment
- "What does 86400 mean?" - Add magic number explanation
- "Is this logged for audits?" - Add `// AUDIT:` annotation
- "Does RLS protect this?" - Add `// RLS:` annotation
